arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a Blazor Web App for logistics/shipment tracking. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-3b13547ed7454ea7ba1a0d06687f7249/ShipmentTracker/` using `dotnet new blazor -o ShipmentTracker -int Auto -ai -au Individual`.

## Project Structure
- **Server project**: `/tmp/sv-3b13547ed7454ea7ba1a0d06687f7249/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker/`
- **Client project**: `/tmp/sv-3b13547ed7454ea7ba1a0d06687f7249/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client/`
- Auto mode, Global interactivity, Individual auth already configured
- EF Core with SQLite, ASP.NET Core Identity already set up in `Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs`

## What to implement

### 1. Remove template pages
Delete these files from the `.Client/Pages/` folder:
- `Counter.razor`
- `Weather.razor`
- `Auth.razor`

### 2. Create shared models in `.Client` project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Cancelled
}

public class ShipmentSummary
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedAtUtc { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDeliveryUtc { get; set; }
    public string? RecipientName { get; set; }
}
```

### 3. Create service interface in `.Client` project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<ShipmentSummary>> GetShipmentsAsync(string? statusFilter = null);
    Task<ShipmentSummary?> TrackShipmentAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<ShipmentSummary> UpdateStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus newStatus);
}
```

### 4. Create client-side service implementation

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient http) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<ShipmentSummary>> GetShipmentsAsync(string? statusFilter = null)
    {
        var url = "/api/shipments";
        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(statusFilter))
            url += $"?status={Uri.EscapeDataString(statusFilter)}";
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<ShipmentSummary>>(url) ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentSummary?> TrackShipmentAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var response = await http.GetAsync($"/api/shipments/track/{Uri.EscapeDataString(trackingNumber)}");
        if (response.StatusCode == System.Net.HttpStatusCode.NotFound)
            return null;
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentSummary>();
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentSummary> UpdateStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus newStatus)
    {
        var response = await http.PutAsJsonAsync($"/api/shipments/{id}/status", newStatus);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentSummary>()
            ?? throw new InvalidOperationException("Failed to deserialize updated shipment.");
    }
}
```

### 5. Register HttpClient and services in Client Program.cs

Edit `ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs` to add:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization();

builder.Services.AddScoped(sp =>
    new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress) });
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentHttpService>();

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

### 6. Create server-side Shipment entity and DbContext changes

Create `ShipmentTracker/Data/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Cancelled
}

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }

    [MaxLength(50)]
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [MaxLength(200)]
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [MaxLength(200)]
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }

    public DateTime CreatedAtUtc { get; set; }

    public DateTime? EstimatedDeliveryUtc { get; set; }

    [MaxLength(200)]
    public string? RecipientName { get; set; }
}
```

Edit `ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs`:
```csharp
